  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.1.0: serializes with Jakar.Json only (built on Jakar.Extensions 10.11.0); Newtonsoft.Json, System.Text.Json and Npgsql.Json.NET are gone. Records are [JsonModel] types: ITableRecord<TSelf> requires IJsonSerializable<TSelf> (the generated ToJson/FromJson/TryFromJson replace TableRecord.FromJson/TryFromJson, and ToString() is the record as JSON). PairRecord.AdditionalData (and ResxRowRecord.AdditionalData) is a JObjectNode? marked [JsonOverflow]: unknown JSON members collect there and are written back. IPairRecord<TSelf> implements IJsonModel; WithAdditionalData takes JObjectNode?. JNode values bind to SQL parameters, batch commands and binary COPY as JSON text, and JNode-typed properties map to json columns. JsonSqlHandler and DbDataReader.GetData need IJsonSerializable<TValue>. JsonResult<TValue> writes the value's runtime [JsonModel] type (JsonCodecRegistry) and throws NotSupportedException for other types. JwtParser reads the payload with Jakar.Json: every claim is returned, and array roles become one claim each. EmailSettings is a [JsonModel]. CommandParameters and its renderers moved to Jakar.SqlBuilder (namespace Jakar.SqlBuilder); SqlParameter is now Jakar.SqlBuilder.CommandParameter. TableMetaData/ColumnMetaData implement ISqlCommandTable/ISqlCommandColumn; record ids implement ISqlParameterValue and bind as their Guid/long (AutoRecordID values were bound as the struct before). CommandParameters.Create<TSelf>(), AddGroup<TSelf>, Validate<TSelf>, ToPostgresParameter and ToSqlParameter are extension members in Jakar.Database. New: ToSqliteParameter, ToMySqlParameter and ToDbParameter(DbCommand) (any ADO.NET provider, typed with the new ColumnMetaData.AdoDbType), with DbColumnType.ToDbType/ToSqliteType/ToMySqlDbType; SqlCommand.ToCommand also dispatches SQLite and MySQL connections and falls back to any DbConnection. All conversions send null as DBNull.Value.",
